    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44714" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπᾰτρις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>,
			ἡ, fem. of foreg., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>born of a noble sire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1077
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἂν εὔ. ὧδε
			βλάστοι</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1081
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίδων . .
			εὐπατρίδων</span> of hopes <i>derived from those of noble
				birth</i>, dub. cj. ib.<i><span class="en">
				858
			</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδᾶν</span> vel -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδῶν</span> codd.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Rome, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ εὐπάτ
				ριδες ἀρχαί</span>
			<i>magistratus patricii</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				46.45
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνὴ εὔ</span>., =
			Lat. <i>patricia</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				72.5
			</span></i> (here acc. sg. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδα</span>, but cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόπατρις,
		ὁμόπατρις</span>).</div>
